# Mutually-exclusive flag combinations are rejected at flag-parse time,
# BEFORE any file read, with exit 1 and canonical-shape stderr.
# This fixture covers `--query` + `-f` → flag.conflict.
# Separate fixtures cover editor conflicts, backup requirements, and
# the dry-run/check conflict.

# --query + -f: only one query source is allowed.
#
# CRITICAL: this rejection MUST happen before any file read. We set the
# file to a nonexistent path and assert the error is the flag.conflict,
# NOT an IO error. That proves the check fires at flag-parse time.
! nesdit does-not-exist.json --query '.' -f q.jq
stderr '^nesdit: error: flag\.conflict: '
! stderr 'does-not-exist'
! stderr 'io\.read'
! stdout .

-- q.jq --
.z = 99
